    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, those are a good start. \n\nI'm a bit worried about the contrast, though. For the \"Early Human Ingenuity\" part, I don't want it to sound too \"mystical\" or like it's just about people living in harmony with nature, if that makes sense? I want to avoid that trope where indigenous tech is treated as almost spiritual or instinctual rather than actual scientific thought. \n\nAt the same time, for the \"Modern Civilization\" part, I want to avoid making it sound like everything \"started\" only when Europe got involved. Can you rewrite them? I'd like the first one to emphasize the technical complexity and systematic logic of traditional tools, and the second one to focus more on the specific mechanical and mathematical advancements without making it sound like a total departure from human history.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
