      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better, thanks. I like the shift toward \"engineering\" and \"systematic logic.\"\n\nOne last thing—I'm looking at the transition between these two sections. I want to make sure the exhibit doesn't accidentally imply a hierarchy where one is 'primitive' and the other is 'advanced.' \n\nCould you write a short transitional paragraph that bridges the two? I want it to explain how we move from these localized, traditional systems of knowledge to the large-scale, standardized global systems of the modern era. I'm trying to avoid the implication that the older ways were just \"simpler\" versions of what came later, and instead frame it as a shift in scale and methodology. Maybe touch on how the approach to knowledge itself changed—from something more integrated with local environments to something more abstract and universal?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
